Ripple Labs owns the largest share of XRP — about 37–42% of the total 100 billion supply — mainly held in escrow, while founders like Chris Larsen (~2.5–5 billion XRP) and major 
exchanges such as Binance and Bithumb (around 1.7–1.8 billion XRP each) also hold significant amounts.
Overview
XRP was created in 2012 with a fixed supply of 100 billion tokens. There is no mining, so ownership depends entirely on initial allocations, escrow releases, and market activity. 
The XRP Ledger allows public verification of wallet balances, making ownership distribution transparent.

Major XRP Holders
1. Ripple Labs (Largest Holder)
Controls ~37–42% of total supply.
Escrow: ~32–45 billion XRP locked in monthly-release escrows.
Operational wallets: ~1–5 billion XRP.
Ripple-linked wallets occupy most of the top positions on the XRP rich list.
